# What an artifact does NOT commit.

# READ THIS BEFORE COPYING A RULE FROM THE TOOLING REPOSITORY'S .gitignore.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE INVERSE OF THAT ONE ON THE ONE RULE THAT MATTERS, and the
# inversion is deliberate rather than an oversight to be tidied up:
#
#   TOOLING REPOSITORY   ignores results/, because that repository produces no
#                        measurements. Anything appearing under results/ there
#                        is a stray output, not evidence.
#   AN ARTIFACT (HERE)   TRACKS results/, because a tracked machine-written file
#                        under results/ is the thing CHECK-07 verifies, and it
#                        verifies it with `git ls-files` rather than with "the
#                        file exists". An artifact whose results/ is ignored has
#                        no evidence at all -- it FAILS the check, silently, and
#                        the failure looks like a checker bug rather than a
#                        missing commit.
#
# So: THERE IS NO `results/` LINE IN THIS FILE, and adding one would break the
# artifact contract. This paragraph exists because a later author copying rules
# between the two repositories is overwhelmingly likely to carry that one line
# in the wrong direction.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments. The pinned, hash-installed environment is rebuilt from
# requirements.txt; the installed tree is never evidence.
.venv/
venv/

# SECRETS. Never committed, in any form. An artifact is a directory an
# interviewer may be handed.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# LANDED DATA AND DERIVED CORPORA -- a licence rule, not a size rule.
#
# Derived corpora are NEVER redistributed. An artifact ships the extraction
# script and the frozen id lists so the set can be REBUILT, plus the source's
# own attribution block. It does not ship the source's material, however
# convenient that would be.
#
# This is enforced and not merely documented: finalize.py FAILS when a landed
# data file is tracked. The rules below keep the common shapes out of the index
# in the first place, so that guard is a backstop rather than the only line.
data/
raw/
corpus/
downloads/
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.parquet
*.jsonl
*.csv
*.xml
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Model weights and caches. Large, re-downloadable, and not evidence.
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx
.cache/
hf_cache/

# Checker reports are written OUTSIDE the artifact by default, because the
# checker must not mutate what it checks: a report written inside becomes an
# input to any hash over this tree and shows up in git status, which then needs
# a permanent exclusion rule someone will forget. This line covers the case
# where a reader deliberately opts into an in-artifact report.
.reports/

# The frozen id lists are the exception to the data rules above and ARE
# committed -- they are what makes the derived set rebuildable. Re-included
# explicitly, after the broad rules, so ordering does not decide the outcome.
!ids/
!ids/**
!**/*.ids.txt

# results/raw/ is the SECOND exception, and it is the one that bites silently.
#
# `raw/` in the licence block above is a rule about SOURCE CORPORA, and a bare
# directory pattern matches at ANY depth -- so it also caught results/raw/,
# which is where runmeta.raw_dir() writes the PER-ITEM RUN RECORDS. Two
# different meanings of the word "raw" collided, and the header of this very
# file insists results/ must be tracked.
#
# MEASURED in a throwaway git repository carrying this file verbatim:
#   git check-ignore -v results/raw/item-0001.json
#     -> .gitignore:56:raw/    results/raw/item-0001.json      (IGNORED)
#   git add -A then staged:  .gitignore, results/figures.json  (records absent)
#
# Why that is worse than it looks: CHECK-07 asks whether a machine-written file
# under results/ is TRACKED, and figures.json is -- so CHECK-07 PASSES while the
# per-item records verify.py re-walks to re-derive that very figure are missing
# from the index. The check stays green while the property it stands for is
# broken, and a handed-over artifact cloned fresh cannot verify its own chain.
#
# Re-included after the broad rules, same discipline as the ids block above. The
# licence rule is UNTOUCHED: a top-level raw/ source tree is still ignored by
# line 56, which was re-confirmed against the same probe after this change.
!results/raw/
!results/raw/**

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
